                            <comment id="17872675" author="JIRAUSER306292" created="Sun, 11 Aug 2024 09:56:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=arunkc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;arunkc&quot;&gt;arunkc&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Hello. I&apos;ve reproduced the bug. It appears that this error occurs when the notebook files are not formatted in the expected JSON format, such as &quot;Mac OS X 2q&#65533;ATTR&#65533;&#65533;&#65533;com.apple.provenance&#1349;88DH/&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Could you check if the files where you are seeing this error are located in the &quot;/zeppelin/notebook&quot; path and verify if they contain such corrupted data? Additionally, it would be helpful if you could check if these files start with a &apos;.&apos; (hidden files)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17872812" author="JIRAUSER306521" created="Mon, 12 Aug 2024 08:47:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=seungyoung.dev&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;seungyoung.dev&quot;&gt;seungyoung.dev&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Hi, I couldn&apos;t find the corrupted files within the path you mentioned, ie &quot;/zeppelin/notebook&quot;. But as shown in the screenshot I have shared before in the UI the file names are there. And the corrupted file names starts with a &apos;.&apos; as well.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17873800" author="reamer" created="Thu, 15 Aug 2024 06:20:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Closed via &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4792&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4792&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
